{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you shall not go up by steps upon My altar</b> — Since He began to give commandments concerning the altar, He completed its commandment and did not defer it until He would command the matters of the offerings in the Torah of the Priests. This is a proof for the words of the Sages and requires no reinforcement. The reason for the steps is the reverence for the altar and its honor, for the glory of HaShem. And the commandments of HaShem have many reasons in each one, for in each one there are many benefits for the body and for the soul."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:12:14.175811185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}